1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,550
The first promise of the fifth arc was made on a Sunday, near the bottom of a hill, under the roof of a station cafe.

2
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:12,624
“We proceed through the exchange office,” Aisha said.

3
00:00:12,624 --> 00:00:26,486
“Through, not around.” A visa, a tight connection, and a loose plan were the whole of it, and the run of the first week was worse than any of them had feared.

4
00:00:26,486 --> 00:00:30,665
The field was new, and the industry was not.

5
00:00:30,665 --> 00:00:41,767
An immigrant family ran a parking service near the airline counter; their van, their bike, and their carriage were the only transport for a hundred metres.

6
00:00:41,767 --> 00:00:46,901
“A cab is not a decoration,” the mistress of the house said.

7
00:00:46,901 --> 00:00:49,655
“It is a roof.”

8
00:00:49,655 --> 00:00:57,493
The distant hills were on the television in the lounge, and the overhead lights of the carriage stayed on all night.

9
00:00:57,493 --> 00:01:04,741
“A homeless man understands the interior of a station better than any engineer,” she said.

10
00:01:04,741 --> 00:01:09,000
“That is a familiarity we cannot buy.”

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:21,057
The bark of a dog, a procession of claps, and the countdown to a spacecraft launch: the cafe television had everything except the freight timetable.

12
00:01:21,057 --> 00:01:34,049
“It is ridiculous,” Lin said, “that a starter can find the fuel but not the train.” The trip, for him, was over before it began.

13
00:01:34,049 --> 00:01:44,561
They would relax for one evening, then smash the last problem: a hijack of the schedule by a cruiser of tourists who had bought every seat.

14
00:01:44,561 --> 00:01:49,310
“Any business has a special month,” Aisha said.

15
00:01:49,310 --> 00:02:10,465
“This is ours, and it matters particularly to the office in the capital.” A note in the margin said: “I must say that we are still far from the offer.”, and it is likely that the baggage rules will change today; a passenger cannot comprehend a rule that the staff themselves cannot restrain.

16
00:02:10,465 --> 00:02:19,007
It was possible that a ragged timetable would never be intimate with a stranger's need; the trip had taught them that much.

17
00:02:19,007 --> 00:02:30,090
A distant hill, a tight connection, and a loose plan: the pattern of the whole arc was already visible in the first Sunday afternoon of the journey.

18
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:37,337
It was, in the end, a promise about the use of a timetable.
